<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Central Puerto Q3 net down to $5.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Central Puerto Q3 net down to $5.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period to Sept 30.</p>
<p>Shr $0.06 vs $0.07</p>
<p>ADR $0.31 vs $0.34</p>
<p>Net $5.5 million vs $6.0 million</p>
<p>Revs $85.5 million vs $71.5 million</p>
<p>Nine mths</p>
<p>Shr $0.24 vs $0.33</p>
<p>ADR $1.18 vs $1.67</p>
<p>Net $20.8 million vs $29.6 million</p>
<p>Revs $245.0 million vs $223.0 million  </p>
<p>NOTE: the firm said the third quarter net was only half a million dollars lower than that of the corresponding period a year ago despite the negative effect of a rise in income tax charged to the nine months accumulated period and paid in the third quarter; a non-recurring loss for corporate bonds repurchase; and the cost of restructuring payroll, all of which make a total of $2.9 million.</p>
<p>Central Puerto is operated and controlled by Chilean utilities Chilgener and Chilquinta.</p>
<p>-- Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650</p>
</text>
